>finding out if there is 3rd party memory out there that anyone has had good
>experience with.  Hopefully, I can get more memory for the allocated amount
>of $'s.

Buy Clearpoint memory.  It's just as good as DEC's, and they have a
lifetime warranty.  I've installed 8MB extra in two 5000-120's with no
problems.

The price is pretty predictable: about 1/2 of what DEC charges for the
same memory.  For instance, DEC's price for the 8MB extra (part no.
MS01-AA, 2x) was $1760, $1000.04 with our educational discount.
Clearpoint's equivalent (part no. DCME-D31, 4x) was $560.  There's no
need to spend the extra money, no matter what DEC's sales reps tell you.

	Darrin
