There is a whole series of "Digital Network Architecture Phase IV xxxxxxxx
Protocol Functional Description" manuals available from DEC.  These describe
the protocols at the various layers.  They do not describe how they are
implemented in any particular host o/s.  

You might want to scrounge up authorization to go to DECUS this Fall in
Anaheim, at least to the extent of Sunday the 8th of December, and attend the
full-day seminar "A Day of DECnet-VAX Internals" (S386). Unfortunately, the
pre-registration deadline has passed, but this seminar is not normally full.
I've attended it in the past and it is excellent. The handout alone is worth
the price of admission; it contains information available from NO other source.

You can call the DECUS office at (508) 841-3511 for details on walk-in seminar
registration -- they should at least be able to tell you whether that seminar
is full, cancelled, or has seats available.  Walk-in price for the seminar 
is $370; for symposium week, $750. 

Failing that, ask around Mitre Corp. -- someone there must have attended that
seminar in the past.  

