 * > I am trying to add a second Interlan 1010 ethernet interface to a
 * > Vax785 running 4.3BSD Unix.  I have configured it as:
 * 
 * > # Interlan ethernet controller
 * > device		il0	at uba? csr 0164000	vector ilrint ilcint
 * > device		il1	at uba? csr 0164020	vector ilrint ilcint
 * 
[ tried different boards, still doesn't work.  device info at boot time is ]

 * > 	il0 at uba0 csr 164000 vec 440, ipl 15
 * > 	il0: hardware address 02:07:01:01:b9:bb
 * > 	il1 at uba0 csr 164020 vec 460, ipl 15
 * 

[ system hangs here... ]

One such problem I had while setting up il0 and il1 was that the DIP
switches on the board were mapped to the same address.  Be SURE that the
address on the second board is (1) different and (2) mapped to what the
system *thinks* it is mapped to.  Also, as der Mouse points out, you
might try mapping the second one to 165000 instead of 164020.  When I
did this, I just flipped the switches to something "different" and it
worked...

 * 
 * > Has anyone tried running more that one Interlan card?
 *

We don't run with one because it exhibited some problems, but I suspect
now that they were *routing* problems and not *hardware* problems, and
we may just reconfigure it to run on both nets.

Also, as from der Mouse, be sure you have the interrupt vectors set such
that they don't conflict with other hardware (such as, say, a tty
multiplex board).
