Not too long ago, I posted asking for opinions on what vendors to look
at for IBM to VAX connectivity, and got an almost unanamous (so I cant
spell) vote for Interlink. Today I spoke at length with a representitive
from Interlink, and we discovered a few things...

(note this is in no way derogatory to Interlink or any company mention,
just facts as they are in our case)

The product that Interlink sells is called DATAStore 1000, which
will let IBM 34x0 tape drives seem as locally connected drives
to the VAX. The VAX host must be running DECnet (not a problem)
and the IBM host must be running either MVS or VM. Problem.

We run DOS/VSE on our IBM ES/9000. Before we upgraded to an ES/9000,
we did run DOS/VSE under VM on a 4381, but with the Prism software
of the ES/9000, that is no longer required. We are (happy) dumping
VM totally, and will be running ES/9000 LPARs (same concept as
VM). The Interlink software cant run on just a DOS/VSE host...

An option would be to create an LPAR on the ES/9000 to run
VM, and let that handle the Interlink software. But that is
totally unfeasable. The cost justifications to doing this
are out of this world. We would be better of purchasing 
DECs version of the 3480, the TU/TA90, for $100k or more...

What I need, hopefully fast, is something that will do what
the Interlink product does, but under DOS/VSE. 

Another option would be to run an AIX parition on the ES/9000,
with TCP/IP and run TCP/IP on the VAX. But from what I understood
that product is still in the developmental stages. And also, 
cost justifications on two sides now. No longer running DECnet,
which our software expects, and running TCP/IP, and then the
cost of licenseing AIX from IBM for an ES/9000...

Help!

Billy D'Augustine
Azog-Thoth@cup.portal.com


