Help!

The University Computer Club at the University of Western Australia was
provided with two surplus VAXes (an 11/750 and 11/730) by the Department of
Electronic Engineering at UWA early in 1991.  We have been running the
750 on-and-off for that time (off when things like the 2.5Volt power
supply failed - it took us almost a month to determine and solve the
problem), but the 730 has what appears to be a problem with it's
Integrated Drive Controller that we haven't been able to solve yet.

We have some technical documentation for the machines, with the
noticeable exception of the RA81 hard-disk subsystem.

Our most recent problem is the RA81 drive on the 750.  Several days ago,
the cooling fan for the drive's spindle motor died.  This caused some
reliability problems in the short term (reality problems in things like
Moria).  When we realised what was wrong, we replaced the fan, but found
that the drive was only reliable for between 2 and 8 hours, when it
ceased reading or writing to the disk.  After several hours off, it
would work again for a short time.

At this point, we ran the on-board RA81 diagnostics and recieved the
following error message:

%RA81-TEST: SUBTEST:0A ERROR:3A UNIT:000
%RA81-FRU-MICRO, SDI-CONTROLLER:

Can anyone help?

We're a little out of our depth on this one...


