In article <1991Nov16.143132.2079@spcvxb.spc.edu>, havemann_l@spcvxb.spc.edu writes:
> If you have another controller or cable, you can try swapping the parts around, 
> I'm not sure if you want to try swapping the MP module - different rev levels 
> may not be compatible - Terry? any suggestiuons?

  First, in order to properly run the tests you'll need to have both port
buttons (A & B) out and the drive not write protected. If you still get the
error, then it wants you to try swapping the processor card (the big one in
the bottom of the upper deck), and if that doesn't work, swapping the SDI
board (the right-hand swing-out board).

  You should only substitute boards of the same rev, unless you've got a copy
of the interoperability matrix handy.

  You should also check the two 3.5" fans in the front of the card cage and
the air filter behind the front bezel. Also, you might check the spindle
drive belt for glazing or cracks.

