We are getting a very strange freeze problem on our Vax after a VMS upgrade.

Immediately after a VMS upgrade, intermittently, several times a day, our
DECNET would cause all processes doing something with Decnet, for example,
setting host, running any command in NCP, to freeze, and go into RWAST
state.  This would happen to all accounts, not just a single account.  When
this happens, sometimes our TGV Multinet V2.2 TCP/IP communications also
stops working.  You can't telnet, and mail is stuck.  But the Multinet
doesn't cause your process to go into RWAST state.  The hardware is a
Vax 11/785.  The current VMS version is 5.3.  The VMS system disk was
copied from a Vax 11/780, which doesn't have this problem at all.  The
exact same code, was backed up with an image backup, and copied to 
the Vax 11/785, where the Decnet freezes.  When we do a show memory
and use monitor, there is no apparent bottleneck in the system causing
the problem.  The output of these commands seems ok.  We have fine tuned
the system significantly using selected sysgen parameters, and autogen.
The fine tuning seems ok.  We have upgraded the DECNET ethernet controller
board to the latest, F2 version.  Since the post upgrade tuning and 
followup work, the freeze has occured less often.  Before the freeze mode
happened every day.  Now it happens about once every three weeks, or a month.

Once again, in synopsis, intermittently, the Decnet goes into a state that
causes all accounts and processes that work with it to freeze.  The machine
continues to function fine, otherwise.  

