The key word being "supported".  If you don't have too much junk in the
backplane, a
BA23 can power two RD drives (I've got an RD53 and RD54 in the same
box).

The 6 button panel would be nice, but I was too cheap to buy it.  If
your electronically
able, pull the BA23 front panel off.  Pins 1&2 of the 20 pin connector
are the drive ready
and write protect for drive 0; pins 5&6 are drive ready/write protect
for drive 1.  Use
3.9k resistors to pull each of these two lines to +5V, and drive 1 will
be ready and 
write enabled.

Good luck.
Hugh.


