In article <8NOV91.10534806@edison.ucsc.edu>, wipke@edison.ucsc.edu writes:
> The above error appears on an RA81.  The red FAULT light goes on,
> and the lights inside read 00110101.  I presume this means the disk
> is a candidate for a landfill project or a ships anchor?

  It could be any number of things. The inside lights are non-deterministic for
errors like this. First, push the red FAULT button. You'll get a pattern of
lights on the front panel. Record the On/Off status of each from left to right.
Next, open the top of the drive (using an Allen wrench). You'll see a DB-25
connector near the right rear. Plug a terminal in there - it's either 300 or
1200 baud. Make sure both A and B port buttons are out and type ^C on the ter-
minal. You should get a prompt. Type DIAG<CR>. Record what it says. If you
don't get any errors, spin the disk up and DIAG again. Mail me all of the info
you've collected and I'll give you some suggestions about what might be wrong.

