>   Now I want to run a simulation program called FIDAP,
>   but it was not possible to acess more than 24 MB 
>   memory. My swap space have 70 MB. What I have done 
>   wrong ? Are there special parameters in the kernel 
>   config file ? Who can help me - please send me a mail. 
>   I am waiting in hope !
>
>        Oliver

config file:

>ident		"IKEDC1"
>machine		mips
>cpu		"DS5000"
>maxusers	32
>processors	1
>maxuprc		50
>physmem		64
>timezone	-1 dst 4
>maxdsiz		64
>smmax		1024
>
>options		LAT
>options		QUOTA
>options		INET


If you enter the 'limit' command in the C-shell, I would suspect that
it returns something like the following

	cputime         unlimited
	filesize        unlimited
	datasize        24576 kbytes
	stacksize       512 kbytes
	coredumpsize    0 kbytes
	memoryuse       unlimited

The trouble is that the datasize per process is too low.  To increase
the datasize value, add the following to your kernel configuration
file and recompile and install a new kernel.

maxdsiz	  200

This will allow a datasize of apprx. 204 kbytes, larger than what you
can currently use with 70mb of swap, but it will solve your problem.
