Gentlepeople,

Many Thanks to those who replied: Dan, John, Ken and Michael

I played around with the Pro 350 after posting the message and came to the
conclusion that:

A/ Rebooting RT-11 after power up pacified RT-11 so it would look at the
   controller.

B/ RT-11 V5.5 raced through the cylinders.  It probably had an error on
   each cylinder so it would skip to the next cylinder. ie NBG format.

C/ RT-11 V5.2 with V5.1 format formatted the RD51 and RD50 head by head.
   (The drive seeked to track zero 4 times) 

D/ The controllers I have will format RD50, RD51, RD52 and RD31.

Now the replies:

From:	IN%"ddl@burrhus.harvard.edu"
>	I had similar problems on a 380.  Sometimes the board would
>show bad on power up, sometimes it would not.  Some subset of the
>times it showed good on power up, it could format a drive.  More
