drack@titan.tsd.arlut.utexas.edu (Dave Rackley) writes:
|>Anybody remember the qio call to simulate 'set term/pasthru' for VMS?
|>
|>Thanks in advance.

To perform the same function as a "SET TERMINAL/PASTHRU", you'll need to
use the IO$_SENSEMODE to get the current characteristics, then, after
setting the TT2$V_PASTHRU bit, use IO$_SETMODE to update the terminal
characteristics.

If what you're trying to do is a "this QIO only" type operation,
IO$_READVBLK with the IO$M_NOFILTR modifier, or IO$_WRITEVBLK with the
IO$M_NOFORMAT modifier, may be what you're looking for.

Keep in mind that this is from memory, so check the I/O Drivers
Reference manual before you write the actual code.

--
