Reminds me of an experience I had many moons ago with an 1/750.

We had a DMR11 in the unibus backplane that was adjacent to the CPU/memory
backplace.  Along with this DMR, there were DZ11s (yuk!), printer controllers,
etc.  Everything worked, except for the DMR.  DEC tried both DMR modules, 
reconfiguring the backplane, to no avail.  As a last desperate act, they
replaced the unibus jumper from the memory backplane.  That fixed it.  Still
don't know why the only thing affected was the DMR.

