> I have heard people mention a VAXstation II/RC.  How does that VAXstation
> differ from say a VAXstation II/GPX?

It was identical to the standard VAXstation II in a BA23 box with the
following exceptions:

    1) It originally came with 3 MB of memory instead of 2 MB
    2) It cost $15,000 instead of $25,000
    3) The badge said "VAXstation II/RC"
    4) It did not include a DECnet license
    5) The last three slots of the H9278 backplane were filled
       with epoxy.   Honest.   I can show you one.

The full configuration included CPU, 3MB memory, DEQNA, RQDX3,
RD53, TQK50, TK50, QVSS (VCB01), VR260, keyboard, mouse (old style).

The "/RC" was supposed to mean "Restricted Configuration", but
I contend that it really stood for "Resin Cured".   :-)

About this same time, DEC removed the H9278 backplane from the
price book, but not before several (many?) people ordered them
(for ~$250).   A few third-party vendors came out with equivalent
backplanes for about the same price.

Mine is still working fine, but has been transplanted to a larger
BA123 box (with lots more memory and peripherals).   I'm still running
the VWS windowing software because DECwindows is too slow to be
useful (and I hear that Motif is even worse).

