From what I recall, there's a 6-button front panel available for [insert
outrageous price here] that will make the 2nd drive go ready.  There is also
apparently a way to do this by inserting a jumper or two behind the existing
4-button front panel, but I don't have the full dope on it.  I'm sure someone
does, though, and I'd like to know too.  That's a hint...

>(b) To do the above, the TK50's gotta go.  I've just picked up a scrap
>DECmate III (sans disk drives, monitor & keyboard), partly as spares for
>my working III+ and partly as a potential drive holder (it has space
