I think the "2nd drive in external box" idea will work fine.  It is, after all,
the way you'd have the drive connected if you used an RQDXE.  I would *not* try
to pull power from the supply in the BA23, since it's near capacity already.
I would, in fact, get longer drive cables and put the 2nd RDxx in the external
box and relieve some of the strain on the internal supply.  You should have no
problems as long as both supplies are on the same circuit...I believe you can
run into floating ground problems if the supplies are on different circuits
(anyone?).

>(c) If a decent sized MFM drive were to unexpectedly turn up on my
>doorstep, does anyone have the good oil on formatting the sucker for use
>with the RQDX3?  Terry?

The DEC "customer diagnostics" TK50 has the "Customer Disk Drive Formatter" on
it, and this should do nicely.  You may have to match the rev of the RQDX3 and
the tape, since I've occasionally had problems with, for instance, the 1988
version of the tape and a lower-rev RQDX3.

You'll have to set one jumper on the drive.  I *believe* the one that needs to
be installed is DS2.  It's been awhile...

