>   How does the DECserver 300 terminal server stack up against other 
>   LAT-TCP/IP terminal servers on the market?

If, like me, you were expecting a terminal server to behave exactly
like a hard-wired line, with full control of parity and baud rate from
the host side, you'll be sadly disappointed.  Ultrix "stty" commands
that set parity and baud rate on LAT ports are ignored.  Well, not
quite ignored -- sometimes you can set the baud rate, but 99% of the
time it doesn't work.  I posted 4 bugs last April; here's one of them.
It's for the DS200, but I have the same problems with the DS300.

Newsgroups: comp.unix.ultrix
Subject: DECserver 200 baud rate not set consistently by Ultrix 4.1 tip command
Date: Wed, 24 Apr 1991 03:24:30 GMT

I have an Ultrix /dev/tty21 LAT port configured to connect to a DS200
autobaud LAT port, but when I specify this in /etc/remote for "tip":

    ty:dv=/dev/tty21:br#2400:pa=even:

tip connects to the port but does not set the parity or the baud rate of
the port.  Actually, rarely and in circumstances I've not been able to
reproduce consistently, it does set the baud rate, but never the parity. 
99% of the time, the baud rate remains at "4800".

Looks like a race condition to me.  Makes using tip and uucp through my
autobauding modem impossible.  I have to sign on to the DECserver and
manually set the port before using tip.

