reads and unlock writes, and where the node to which an interlock read
is addressed responds to the receipt of the command with an ACK at a
fixed time after the command, and then arbitrates for the bus and
responds to the command an unspecified number of cycles later with one
type response if the memory location is locked and another type of
response containing the requested read data if it is unlocked.

